      ro: "Wuxi, situat Ã®n provincia Jiangsu pe malul nordic al lacului Tai, este un oraÈ™ industrial major cu o identitate culturalÄƒ profund Ã®nrÄƒdÄƒcinatÄƒ. OraÈ™ul este adesea numit 'Perla Lacului Tai' È™i este traversat de Marele Canal, care a modelat comerÈ›ul È™i transportul timp de secole. Wuxi are o istorie de peste 3.000 de ani È™i a fost un centru pentru mineritul staniului Ã®ncÄƒ din timpul dinastiei Zhou, fapt la care face referire È™i numele sÄƒu ('fÄƒrÄƒ staniu'), dupÄƒ ce resursele au fost epuizate. AstÄƒzi, Wuxi este un centru lider pentru producÈ›ia modernÄƒ, textile È™i tehnologia informaÈ›iei Ã®n Delta Fluviului Yangtze. Din punct de vedere turistic, oraÈ™ul impresioneazÄƒ prin Marele Buddha din Lingshan È™i parcul pitoresc Capul de BroascÄƒ ÈšestoasÄƒ de pe malul lacului. BucÄƒtÄƒria tradiÈ›ionalÄƒ din Wuxi, cunoscutÄƒ pentru aromele sale dulci, È™i faimoasele figurine din argilÄƒ Huishan sunt elemente esenÈ›iale ale moÈ™tenirii regionale. Wuxi Ã®ntruchipeazÄƒ tranziÈ›ia de la un oraÈ™ comercial istoric la o metropolÄƒ de ultimÄƒ generaÈ›ie, fÄƒrÄƒ a-È™i pierde atracÈ›ia peisagisticÄƒ.",
      en: "Wuxi, located in Jiangsu Province on the northern shore of Lake Tai, is a prominent industrial city with a deeply rooted cultural identity. Often referred to as the 'Pearl of Lake Tai,' the city is bisected by the ancient Grand Canal, which has facilitated trade and transport for centuries. Wuxi's history stretches back over 3,000 years; it was a major tin mining center during the Zhou Dynasty, a fact reflected in its name, which literally means 'without tin,' signifying the era when the mines were exhausted. Today, Wuxi stands as a leading hub for advanced manufacturing, textiles, and information technology within the Yangtze River Delta. Its tourism sector is anchored by the colossal Lingshan Grand Buddha and the scenic Yuantouzhu (Turtle Head) Isle on the lake. The city's traditional cuisine, noted for its characteristic sweetness, and the famous Huishan clay figurines are integral parts of its regional heritage. Wuxi exemplifies the seamless evolution from a historic trading town into a cutting-edge metropolis while preserving its natural scenic charm.",
