      en: "Changzhou, situated within the Yangtze River Delta in Jiangsu Province, is a city distinguished by its enduring prosperity and deep cultural heritage. With a history spanning over 2,500 years, Changzhou became a vital stop along the Grand Canal during the Sui Dynasty, which catalyzed its economic development. Today, the city is a premier hub for advanced manufacturing, leading in sectors such as robotics and renewable energy. Often called the 'Dragon City,' Changzhou is home to the Tianning Temple, featuring a pagoda widely recognized as the tallest wooden pagoda in the world. A major modern attraction is the China Dinosaurs Park, a massive theme park that has established the city as a top destination for family tourism. Traditional crafts, most notably the exquisite Changzhou combs, continue to be a cherished part of its local identity. Changzhou effectively bridges its legacy as a historic commercial node with its contemporary focus on high-tech innovation.",
